66:    needs, and when in this course's year. Same-year leans form the availability calendar: which unit of this
67:    course uses it and the earliest unit of the other course that may teach it, so the other subject's frame can
68:    honour it. Where the other subject's frame is not written yet, record the need and do not guess its unit
69:    numbers. A citation of another frame's unit gives its course days as that frame states them
70:    ("math grade 4 unit 3 (days 30 to 47)"); the gate notes a citation more than 3 days off that unit's place in
71:    data/plans/calendar.csv.
