169: ## Rules
170: - The progression rows are the contract: place every owned row, change none. If a row is wrong, list it under "For
171:   the lead" with the fix; do not edit data/progressions/.
172: - Days fit what a unit owns: the read names a unit far over or under its share. Weigh the load notes in the rows,
173:   not equal shares per row.
174: - Sensitive content: name it in the unit's last column with a teacher note, following the lens and the values rule.
175:   No role play or simulation that puts a child in a victim's or perpetrator's place.
176: - No em dashes; "Curio Class" in full; no company names. Edit only your frame files. No git.
177: - Base texts: where the subject has one (IM for math, OpenSciEd for middle school science, EL Education for ELA K to
178:   5), the frame ends with a `## Source map` section: a table placing every base unit (and its lesson range) in one
179:   of the course's units, from the source store (S:\CurioClass-sources) and docs/sources/BASE-TEXTS.md; a base lesson
180:   left out is named with the reason. The day-level data/plans/<course>/source-map.csv comes with the scope and
181:   sequence (step 3), not now.
182: - Stale notes: a note that waits on other work starts `Pending(<file>, <file>#<text> or <plan node>):`; other
183:   work-status wording ("not yet placed", "to come") fails the gate. Run `python -X utf8 scripts/stale.py check`
184:   on your files before finishing.
185: - Run `python -X utf8 scripts/frame.py check <slug>` (the gate: sections, placement, owned standards, days, the
186:   lessons above; `python -X utf8 scripts/frame.py sync` writes data/plans/frames.csv, data/plans/calendar.csv and the
187:   table in docs/courses/CALENDAR.md) and fix every FAIL. Read its notes too: each names a lesson.
188: - Check your own work with a short script in the scratchpad before finishing: every owned skill_id placed exactly
189:   once, every code in Owned standards found in those rows, days in units plus check days equal the total.
190: 
191: Final message, short: per course the units and days, the check result, the "For the lead" items, what you were
192: unsure of.
