ard made on the last making day naming three conditions; MA:Cn10.1.2a, a guide look-for on the kept source card and the piece: what the child knew, liked or read, and an example, named and credited; MA:Pr6.1.2b, a talk item (check day 2): what presenting was like and one result; MA:Cn10.1.2b, a talk item (check day 2): a media experience and what it meant or was for, the child's own or the class-shared one, marked the same. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: an outside source and a source log (grade 3). Tools: the scroll box template, screening-plan card, source card, sound-cue card, Curio Class's own. Free path: a cereal box, two pencils as rollers and taped paper. Once-a-week path: 4 sessions | Last in the band because the screening joins the band's framing, order, recording and placement and ends the year after the year-end check (week 27); the sources thread then goes to grade 3's source log | Candidate: a public domain or openly licensed tale collection with stories from more than one region, so the class's tale choice keeps the year's range | Tales: no sacred or ceremonial story is told; a tale from a culture is told only from its community's own published version, never invented or imitated. Credits: only public domain or openly licensed media in the piece. Hazards and controls: pencil rollers with blunt ends, box edges checked; sound cues at low volume. A family's yes before any showing outside class, under the child's chosen name; no child filmed. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
