277: ## Cross-subject
278: 
279: No media arts row of grades K to 2 carries a cross_subject lean (data/progressions/arts.csv), so this course waits
280: on no other course and no other course waits on it. The contacts below are practiced, not owned, each with its "if
281: later" line; all are core courses (lesson 32).
282: 
283: ### Mathematics, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)
284: 
285: | Used here | Contact | If math has not taught it yet |
286: |---|---|---|
287: | Units 2 and 3 (year K): first, next and last on the storyboard; three picture cards | Counting small sets, in math kindergarten unit 1 (days 1 to 18) | Order is said as first, next and last by pointing; no counting beyond three is asked |
288: | Unit 7 (year 1): a repeat in a six-frame strip | Patterns are not a math standard in K to 2; counting to six is kindergarten math | The repeat is found by looking (the same picture again), never by counting rules |
289: 
290: No unit asks for measuring, fractions, time on a clock, symmetry or scale (lesson 13).
291: 
292: ### English language arts, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)
293: 
294: Talk about media pieces and the critique practice collaborative conversation (SL.K.1, SL.1.1, SL.2.1), and telling a
295: picture-card tale practices retelling with key details: practiced, not owned. If ELA has not yet taught the
296: turn-taking rules, the critique card shows them in pictures (look, listen, one at a time) and the teacher models them
297: on the first critique day.
298: 
299: ### Social studies, kindergarten to grade 2
300: 
301: Unit 9's "life of a time, a place and a people" (year 2) sits near social studies grade 2's unit 6, "Family stories
302: and culture". No lean either way: the art unit teaches the setting it uses itself, on work cards (bar criterion 7),
303: and never asks a child to explain their own family's culture.
304: 
305: ### Computer science (not a core course)
306: 
307: STANDARD.md 6: media arts teaches the one idea of privacy or credit its unit needs in a short step and does not wait
308: for computer science. Here: asking before a picture and no faces (units 1, 5 and 9) and naming a source (units 9 and
309: 12). Computer science goes deeper on attribution in grade 8 (computer-science:g8-attribution); its K to 2 courses
310: are not core, so nothing here assumes them.
