313: 
314: 1. **Media arts connecting ids swapped (settled).** Checked at source (the California standards page for
315:    MA:Cn10 grade 3): anchor 10 is the student's own experience and anchor 11 society, culture and history, as in
316:    every other discipline. The words-file lines for MA:Cn10.1.* and MA:Cn11.1.* were swapped, every ma-*-sources
317:    row now carries the Cn10 ids and every ma-*-society row the Cn11 ids, and this frame's id labels changed to match
318:    (the pairs of rows stay in their units).
319: 2. **Media arts weekly time figure.** STANDARD.md 3.4 has no media arts figure; the visual and media arts
320:    association's elementary checklist (the same file the visual arts pilot read for its 50 minutes) is read at source
321:    for its media arts lines, then the Pending note in the Days bullet is replaced with the figure and the gaps on both
322:    paths.
323: 3. **After-core check weeks.** This frame's checks are in week 21 (mid-year) and week 27 (year-end) in every year,
324:    off every core check week. Week 21 holds no other check today; week 27 shares with theater K to 2 in all three
325:    grades, and with computer science K, health and library K (grade K), computer science 1 and health (grade 1), and
326:    ELD, health and physical education (grade 2). Left for the
327:    lead's one calendar pass. The once-a-week path's respond sessions are in weeks 22 and 28.
328: 4. **Arts disciplines in the stagger check** (as the pilot's item 2): two arts courses in one week are never
329:    flagged while the check keys on subject.
330: 5. **Paper path meets the capture and tool ids (item-level, decided).** I read "media tool" as anything that
331:    frames, captures, orders, plays or shows pictures and sound, so a device-free class meets MA:Cr3.1.Ka, MA:Pr5.1.*
332:    and MA:Pr5.1.2c (recording) in full on paper (a drawn frame, a sound score). If the lead or Cory wants recording
333:    ids met only on a device, the course needs one shared device per group of five, which is a cost question.
