222: | ma-g5-society | Media in the community, ads and their history, and the class checklist for ethical, media-literate use | ma-g6-society (unit 1) | Identity joins the investigation; copyright becomes a rule for the student's own media, on the class card |
223: | ma-g5-ideas | Ideas drawn from others' work; a proposal and model tested for a stated audience | ma-g6-ideas (unit 2) | A chosen creative method; plans, mockups and production steps critiqued against the purpose |
224: | ma-g5-craft | Varied roles practiced; a convention bent; ordinary and experimental tool use compared | ma-g6-craft (unit 2) | Assigned roles performed; constraints tested on purpose; tools used both ways |
225: | ma-g5-make | Parts joined for meaning with emphasis; changes decided for clarity before refining | ma-g6-make (unit 3) | Several approaches tried for a point of view; changes judged for effect before refining for the audience |
226: | ma-g5-judge | Personal and group readings compared; criteria set by the student | ma-g6-judge (unit 3) | Given criteria first, then chosen criteria, for pieces and their production steps |
227: | ma-g5-present | A mixed-content piece; two showing formats weighed; a role taken and results compared | ma-g6-present (unit 4) | Forms blended to back a core message; formats analyzed; a written review replaces the talk |
228: | ma-g5-sources | Sources gathered; news and community events shape cultural experience | ma-g6-sources (unit 4) | Sources weighed for quality, research included; media gives a historical event new meaning |
