role's tasks done and one skill built; MA:Pr5.1.6b, a written item: a new constraint card, two solutions and the one chosen, why; MA:Pr5.1.6c, a written item: a tool from the tray named in one ordinary and one experimental use, and what each gives. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a prototype judged for resources (grade 7). Tools: the planning portfolio, role cards, storyboard sheets, a frame-sequence viewer or its printed flip book, Curio Class's own. Free path: paper flip books, a paper film strip, found objects. Once-a-week path: 9 sessions | After unit 1 because planning a piece needs the parts and techniques just named and the ethics card for any source used; before unit 3 because a point-of-view piece is made from a plan and in roles. The storyboard and production-roles models are retrieved here. Longest unit of the year: five ids, a planning portfolio and a team production | Candidate: a living animator from Africa or Asia beside McCay and McLaren, described and linked, for the year's range | Begone Dull Care changes color fast: the unit plan checks its excerpt against the flash rule (success criterion 2.3.1) and, if it fails, shows still frames and describes the motion. Team work: a student who cannot work in a team holds every role in turn on a solo piece, marked the same. Hazards and controls: lamps low-power and kept off paper, cords taped, blades by an adult only, recording only with the family's yes, screen breaks. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
