nd its production steps, with one constructive suggestion. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: narrative structure (grade 7). Tools: the angle step card, the criteria card, the revision log, Curio Class's own. Free path: a card viewfinder and drawn panels. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | After unit 2 because the sequence is planned with the storyboard and made in the roles just learned; before unit 4 because the screening joins finished work. The revision-log model is retrieved here and the critique-protocol model gains its given and chosen criteria | Candidate: a living maker known for point-of-view shots, from Africa or the Americas, described and linked | Vertov's film was made to show Soviet city life; the unit names its setting in one plain sentence and the agent reads a film archive's page first. The unit plan names its excerpts and leaves out the film's childbirth and bathing scenes. Critique talks about the work, never the maker; students judge only pieces they have permission to share in class. Hazards and controls: filming only in school spaces with the teacher's leave and of things and hands unless a family has said yes; no climbing for a high angle (a high angle is taken from a standing height or drawn); screen breaks. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
