| 1 | K | Media all around us. *Where do we meet media in our day, and what do its parts tell us?* | 18 | ma-k-read; ma-k-society | MA:Re7.1.Ka; MA:Re7.1.Kb; MA:Cn11.1.Ka; MA:Cn11.1.Kb | Responding (Re7); connecting (Cn11); creating practiced through the first viewfinder pictures (review). Works: Eadweard Muybridge, The Horse in Motion (United States, 1878, the Library of Congress, public domain), a row of photographs of one running horse; studio portraits by Seydou Keïta (Bamako, Mali, about 1949 to 1962), described and linked to a holding museum's page, never copied; Hildegard Westerkamp, Kits Beach Soundwalk (Vancouver, Canada, 1989; born 1946 in Germany; the unit plan records whether living, as of its date), a sound piece made on a walk by the sea, described and linked to the artist's own page; the class's own viewfinder drawings and sound map of media in the school (a sign, the bell, a poster, a screen), with no faces | MA:Re7.1.Ka: notice the parts of a media piece (pictures, sounds, words; still or moving) and tell what it seems to say, on Muybridge's row and on school signs. MA:Re7.1.Kb: notice and share how two pieces give different experiences (looking at the horse photographs against listening to the soundwalk with eyes closed). MA:Cn11.1.Ka: with help, share where media shows up in the child's day (the bell, a sign, a song, a picture book read aloud), on a media-hunt walk in the school, with a story character's day offered beside the child's own and marked the same. MA:Cn11.1.Kb: with help, use media tools and spaces safely and politely: the viewfinder and any shared device held in two hands and set down on the table, a turn waited for, asking before pointing at anyone, no picture of a face. Technique: framing with a card viewfinder (hold, look, choose what is inside, draw it); a listening walk with a picture sound map. Words: media, part, message, sound, frame, safe. Showing: the class's "media in our school" wall of viewfinder drawings and sound maps. 