5: q-bar-subjects; see "Decided" and "Still open with Cory" near the end). Not read by the expert since revision.
6: 
7: **Core subjects come first.** This is a soft goal (Cory, 2026-11-11; docs/agents/decisions/BASELINE.md rule 24).
8: Work on the subjects on this page waits behind math, English language arts, science and social studies unless it
9: is complementary, such as a shared rule or a standards fix that serves both. Social studies is core. Every course
10: is still finished to the bar; this sets the order, not the scope.
11: 
12: **What this page is for.** Every one of the 120 courses (118 active, 2 world languages shelved) is to be finished to the adoption bar (docs/FOUNDATION.md,
13: section 4; docs/ADOPTION-BAR.md). Math has a rubric file; English language arts and science rubrics are drafted
14: separately. This page writes the bar for every other subject: one shared core, then a short part per subject.
15: 
16: **What we may never say.** That Curio Class was reviewed by, meets, or is endorsed by any body named here. This is a
17: bar we hold ourselves to. Most instruments are all rights reserved, so nothing is quoted. Every criterion is in our
18: own words.
19: 
20: **What this page is not.** An approach page. Layer 3 asks for one per subject before a scope and sequence, and none exists (see
21: "Before a scope and sequence in this subject"). A subject's part moves to its own docs/RUBRIC-*.md file once it is firm.
